HUMAN: Round 6 analysed — rebuild makeJet() into a world-class procedural fighter; 8 findings, hard contracts listed.
NOTE contracts at=flight-sim3.html:5729-5760#"root.userData.gearNose = gearNose" what="MUST SURVIVE: root.userData anchors {gunL,gunR,missileL,missileR,wingtipL,wingtipR,engineExhaust,gearNose,gearL,gearR,navRed,navGrn,+any others in that block}; gear retract rotates gearNose.rotation.x / gearL|R.rotation.z (12581-12584); gear compression reads grp.userData.{strut,wheel,baseStrutY,baseWheelY} (12593+); castShadow applied by traversal helper at 4373; GLB swap path (loadOptionalPlaneGLB) must still work; afterburner/ab2 + cockpit interior (5314-5369) kept as-is; NO new lights (I5)"
FIND F16 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5070-5086#"// Fuselage — elongated along Z" what="fuselage is bare cylinder+cone; reads toy-grade" fix="single lofted BufferGeometry: ~12 elliptical cross-section stations nose(-8.2) to tailcone(+8.2), wider-than-tall sections with soft chine (superellipse exponent ~2.6 mid-body), radome taper, raised dorsal spine behind canopy fading to tail, smooth normals; replaces fuse+nose meshes; cylindrical UVs for F22 texture" ref=flight-sim3.html:5071-5077#"const fuse = new THREE.Mesh" dep=-
FIND F17 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5137-5144#"// Canopy — stretched half-sphere" what="canopy is scaled half-sphere, flat shading, no frame" fix="teardrop bubble via LatheGeometry profile (windscreen rake into bubble apex into spine fairing), thin frame rails (dark torus arcs / extruded strips), glass material gains generated gradient CubeTexture envMap (6 tiny canvas faces: sky-top to warm-horizon) with envMapIntensity ~1.1, opacity 0.42, roughness 0.06; SAME cubemap applied to matFuse/matDark/wingMat at envMapIntensity ~0.5 for metal reflections" ref=flight-sim3.html:5059-5062#"const matCanopy" dep=F16
FIND F18 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5146-5177#"// --- Wings: swept delta" what="wings are a warped slab box; no airfoil, no LERX" fix="custom airfoil loft: rounded leading edge, cambered upper surface, sharp trailing edge (~6 chord points x 6 span stations), taper+sweep+dihedral preserved from current numbers so handling visuals match; LERX strakes blending wing root forward along fuselage; wingtip missile-rail fairings; keep two-tone vertexColors; static wicks (4 thin dark cylinders on TE); UPDATE anchors: wingtipL/R, gunL/R pods, missileL/R rails re-seated on the new wing (rails/pods keep current world XY within 0.3)" ref=flight-sim3.html:5148#"const g = new THREE.BoxGeometry(11" dep=F16
FIND F19 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5189-5222#"// --- Vertical tail ---" what="fin+stabs are warped boxes" fix="swept trapezoid fin with airfoil thickness, inset rudder shadow-line (thin dark recessed strip), tip antenna fairing pod; all-moving stabs with the same airfoil section as wings, slight anhedral" ref=flight-sim3.html:5203#"const tail = new THREE.Mesh(makeTail(), matFuse)" dep=F16
FIND F20 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5224-5240#"// Engine intakes (sides)" what="intakes are plain boxes with black caps" fix="curved intake bodies (box loft with rounded outer lip), splitter plate gap vs fuselage, dark ramped throat, small boundary-layer diverter; nozzle upgrade folded here: 12 inner petal facets (single lathe with flat shading) + hotter inner ring" ref=flight-sim3.html:5120-5126#"// Engine nozzle" dep=F16
FIND F21 sev=H tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5243-5281#"// --- Landing gear ---" what="gear = single cylinder strut + plain wheel; user singled out the gear" fix="per gear: two-stage oleo (outer strut + polished piston cylinder w/ high metalness), scissor link (2 angled small boxes), drag brace to fuselage, hub with 6 bolt studs (tiny cylinder ring or 6-sided disc), torus tire + brake disc behind wheel, mudguard on nose gear, gear-bay doors (thin panels parented INSIDE each gear group so existing retract rotation animates them free); twin nose wheels; CONTRACT: keep grp.userData.{strut,wheel,side,baseStrutY,baseWheelY} pointing at the load-bearing strut group and rolling wheel mesh so compression+spin code at 12593+ works untouched" ref=flight-sim3.html:12581-12584#"jet.userData.gearNose.rotation.x",flight-sim3.html:12608#"noseWheel" dep=-
FIND F22 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5053-5068#"const matFuse = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial" what="flat untextured materials" fix="one generated 1024x1024 canvas texture shared by fuselage/wings/tail: base two-tone grey camo blocks, panel lines (1px darker strokes on a station grid), rivet dot rows along panels, ELEMENT-115 stencil + roundel + tail code 'E-115', subtle walkway anti-slip strip; used as .map with per-material color tint kept; second small canvas as roughnessMap (panel-line variation); anisotropy 4; textures generated once at build, no fetches" ref=flight-sim3.html:7678#"function makeSpriteTexture" dep=F16,F18
FIND F23 sev=L tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html:5283-5312#"// --- Afterburner glow ---" what="missing believable detail greebles" fix="pitot tube (nose), 2 AoA vanes, 2 blade antennas (spine/belly), formation-light emissive strips (thin toneMapped:false planes, wingtip+fin, opacity tied to existing nav-light logic if trivially reachable else static 0.35), 4 RWR bumps; ALL merged into at most 2 meshes (1 per material) via BufferGeometryUtils-style manual merge or few shared-mat meshes; draw-call budget: net +<=15 draws vs current model, <=9 total materials" ref=flight-sim3.html:5736#"root.userData.navRed" dep=F16,F18
OPEN O5 q="keep current grey+red accent livery or switch to the orange/white Element-115 title livery? assume keep grey airframe with orange-accent stripes (ties to logo, avoids clown-plane)" default=grey-orange-accents
